WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.900
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
10 packages of design know-how.

1
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.420
Every rule in it was
written by somebody else.

2
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.140
Almost every design
decision is already settled.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.400
Contrast: the W3C.
The laws of attention: Jon YABLONSKI.

4
00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:24.759
Colour blindness: a paper from 2009,
measured on real eyes.

5
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:28.879
Published years ago.
Your tools have never heard of any of it.

6
00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:34.359
It is code now, pointed both ways.
At what you make, at what is live.

7
00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:39.919
167 chart kinds.
20 accessibility rules. 30 laws of UX.

8
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.120
The rule that draws the figure
is the rule that audits the page.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.062
A vision model renders the chart
and looks at it.

10
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.520
It says what is wrong.
Then you fix the source.

11
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.680
The model edits the plan.
It never touches the picture.

12
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.775
Then the chart is drawn again.
That is the whole loop.

13
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.999
A matrix, a calendar, a migration flow,
a choropleth. 4 of 167 kinds.

14
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.560
This one is drawn on Equal Earth,
a projection published in 2018.

15
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.960
Everything stays on your desk.
Nothing travels.

16
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.640
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.220
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
